==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*3 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Devil Wife]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*2 [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Condemned Peng]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Mysterious Calamity]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**1 [[Fallen Bear]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 66.67~80 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,400f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 40~53.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Devil Wife|Devil Wives]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 93.33~100 seconds<sup>2,800f~3,000f</sup>.
**2 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to the Mysterious Calamity's high Omni Strike range, most units cannot stay on the field long. Therefore, using disposable units, mostly rushers, is recommended. A few good units for this purpose include [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] is particularly good here due to the main boss being floating. The Devil Wives give a constant stream of money, so it's not really an issue. Less disposable rushers, such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can also work, but they need to get a lot of damage off quickly in order to be worth the slot, money, and cooldown. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can also be very useful here to slow the boss, but be warned that the Fallen Bear's shield allows it to push regardless.

To deal with Fallen Bear, the best shield piercing options are [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] and [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] due to sharing similar traits with the aforementioned disposable rushers.

As for meatshields, not many are needed, as the boss continually wipes the frontline with high enough damage that no meatshield can survive a hit, and the peons don't push too hard on their own. Due to the boss' omnistrike, fast meatshields are a must, including [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]]. Another option is meatshields with the survive ability, such as [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] and, if you have them, [[Kyubey Cat (Rare Cat)|Kyubey Cat]]. You can also use [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]], since most enemies here are slow attackers.

